Referring to the foot-note (ante,                     p.       31), I     remark that the theorem                        7= deficiency, is   absolute,       and applies         to    a curve with any singularities whatever                             :   in       a curve which has singularities not taken account of in Abel's theory, the "quelques cas particuliers que je  me dispense de considdrer," the singularities not taken account of give rise to a diminution in the deficiency of the curve, and also to an equal diminution of the value of 7 as determined by Abel's formula; and the actual deficiency will be = Abel's 7 --- such diminution, that is, it will be = true value of 7.

