\paperheading{ADDITION TO MR GENESE'S NOTE ON THE THEORY OF ENVELOPES}{}

It   is   to   be remarked that writing in the equation of the parabola these values X = 0, /* = 0, 6\textbackslash\{\}textbackslash\textbackslash\{\}\{\textbackslash\{\}\} --- a/i =             successively,   we find respectively

x\textbackslash\{\}\{x --- as) = 0,

y(y-b2) = 0, (bx + ay) (b.e + ay --- ahz) =     ;

viz.    in   each       case    the   parabola reduces itself to a pair of lines, one of the given lines    and a         line      through the intersection of the other two lines; the parallel   thereto parabola thus becomes a curve having a dp on the line at infinity.

In the fourth case z = 0, the equation in        \textbackslash\{\}textbackslash\textbackslash\{\}\{\textbackslash\{\}\}, fi is (\textbackslash\{\}textbackslash\textbackslash\{\}\{\textbackslash\{\}\}y + fix)- = 0, giving a variable value    \textbackslash\{\}textbackslash\textbackslash\{\}\{\textbackslash\{\}\}-i-iJ,   = --- x-\textasciicircum{}y; hence s = 0, the line at infinity is a proper envelope. The true geometrical result is that the envelope consists of the three points A, B. C, and the line at infinity; a point qud curve of the order   and class 1 is not represent- able by a single equation in point-coordinates, and hence the peculiarity in the form of the analytical result.

